ling showing Smith consistently within single digits, or a major late outside-spending push into the district, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 69 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Greg Murphy (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Rep. Greg Murphy seeks another term in this eastern North Carolina district, which leans Republican by about six points at the baseline. He faces Democrat Raymond Smith Jr., a Pitt County official, plus a Libertarian candidate. Murphy has raised roughly ten times what Smith has and holds a large cash advantage, with little outside spending on either side so far.\n\nRatings split between Solid R and Likely R, and prediction markets give Smith roughly a one-in-six chance. The only poll, a Democratic-sponsored August survey of likely voters, showed Murphy ahead just 44-41, hinting the race could be closer than raters suggest. Still, the combination of incumbency, money, and the district's lean makes Murphy the clear favorite, with Smith needing a strong national environment to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0567, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0798, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0901, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1267, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.114, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1275, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1234, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0732, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0908, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-